    "result_text": "The full build passes. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: fiscal-year basis for date-derived values\n\nThe fiscal year starts **1 July** and is identified by the calendar year in which it *ends* (the Australian convention matching this app's AU regions, timezones, and holidays): July\u2013December \u2192 `year + 1`, January\u2013June \u2192 `year`.\n\n**New helper** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/FiscalYear.java`:\n- `of(date)` \u2192 fiscal year as a full year (e.g. 2027)\n- `label(date)` \u2192 `\"FY<YY>\"` (e.g. `FY27`)\n- `elapsed(from, to)` \u2192 whole fiscal years elapsed\n\n**`OwnerMapper`** (`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`):\n- Added `fiscalYear` mapping + `toFiscalYear(owner)` \u2014 `FY<YY>` from the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`, null when absent.\n- `toMembershipNumber` \u2014 year segment (`-M<YY>`) now uses the **fiscal year** of the registration date instead of the calendar year.\n- `toMembershipPoints` \u2014 the +3 tenure award now triggers on **\u2265 1 elapsed fiscal year** (registration's fiscal year earlier than the current one) instead of a `> 365`-day window. A newly created owner still has zero tenure.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` read-only property to the Owner schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it) and updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to describe the fiscal-year basis.\n\nAll values flow from the single business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`, so they stay mutually consistent (e.g. a registration rolled to 2026-09-07 yields `fiscalYear=FY27` and `membershipNumber=\u2026-M27`).\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsFiscalYear` which asserts the `fiscalYear` field matches `FY\\d{2}`.",
